    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a high-upside slate today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the team with an elite 83.29 efficiency score against Luis Severino. The combination of a favorable hitter's park, a +15% SP skill boost, and the primary leadoff spot makes **Gunnar Henderson** our clear anchor. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.99) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.88) follow closely behind; **Jacob Wilson** particularly benefits from a significant +16% park factor adjustment, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** exploits a dynamic platoon advantage against Alcantara. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (69.76) and **Jackson Merrill** (66.29) provide steady production in the heart and top of the order, respectively, as they capitalize on a favorable matchup against Bryce Elder and Kyle Leahy.\n\nStrategic platoon edges and park dynamics are fueling the bottom of the lineup\u2019s viability. **Andy Pages** (61.96) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.02) both clear the 60-point threshold, with **Andy Pages** benefiting from a neutral platoon setting that maximizes his current power output. The most difficult bench decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who posted a 53.67; while his versatility is valuable, he ultimately lost out to the higher-ceiling efficiency of **Josh Jung** (57.34) and the positional requirements of the infield slots. We remain cautious regarding **Liam Hicks** (52.72) and **Drake Baldwin** (53.28); both carry \"Lineup Pending\" tags, and their scores are sensitive to order fluctuations. We are monitoring weather and lineup confirmations for **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** closely, as any deviation from the projected top-of-order slots would necessitate a re-evaluation of their projected efficiency.",
